\subtree[stt-010B]{
  \title{Reflections}

  \p{One of the most obvious places where the library needed improvement was
     in the documentation:
  \ul{
    \li{There is no (easily accessible) 'index' page where you can view
    all the modules. We have since added a link to the Everything.agda on the homepage,
    but there's probably still opportunity to improve here (\Issue{287}).}
    \li{The search feature doesn't work too well at the moment. As far as we can tell,
         Forester currently doesn't support full text search, and
    by default the search is not particularly \em{fuzzy}. It was recently announced
    that the upcoming Forester 6 will
    have a new ocaml-native search feature, and we hope it will be more
    customisable and/or have improved search by default.}
    \li{
    Another search feature that would be nice to have is the ability to search Agda
    definitions directly through the search bar on the site.
    [[martinescardo]] recently made a [very nice tool](https://martinescardo.github.io/TypeTopologySearch.html) for
    searching though the [[TypeTopology]] library from which we could take some inspiration.}
    \li{Relatedly, there are some links in the rendered Agda code
    which don't take you to the correct tree (\Issue{98}), which can make navigating through the
    website quite confusing. This is a bit tricky to fix as the bug stems
    from a mismatch in how Forester and Agda handle unicode.}
  }
  }
}
